Collect the database name on Azure SQL Database when ``query_metrics.disable_secondary_tags`` is enabled. Previously the setting dropped ``database_name`` entirely, which stopped query metrics from resolving the ``azure_sql_server_database`` resource and silently removed the Azure enrichment tags (``cloud_provider``, ``region``, ``resource_group``, ``subscription_id``, ``tenant_name`` and others) in addition to the documented ``db`` tag.
